; Two transactions with the same UUID, the same postings count and the
; same accounts and amounts, but different multiplicities: the earlier
; one posts $1.00 twice, the later one posts $2.00 twice.  They are not
; the same multiset of postings, so the later one is rejected.

2024/01/15 Store
    ; UUID: mult-1
    (Zzz:V)              $1.00
    (Zzz:V)              $1.00
    (Zzz:V)              $2.00

2024/01/15 Store
    ; UUID: mult-1
    (Zzz:V)              $2.00
    (Zzz:V)              $1.00
    (Zzz:V)              $2.00

test bal --columns=80 -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 16:
While comparing this previously seen transaction:
> 2024/01/15 Store
>     ; UUID: mult-1
>     (Zzz:V)              $1.00
>     (Zzz:V)              $1.00
>     (Zzz:V)              $2.00
to this later transaction:
> 2024/01/15 Store
>     ; UUID: mult-1
>     (Zzz:V)              $2.00
>     (Zzz:V)              $1.00
>     (Zzz:V)              $2.00
Error: Transactions with the same UUID must have equivalent postings
end test
